# M2-GROUPED-ADDRESS-ESCAPE (Codex OPUS-CODEX-20261015-12 Q6): `@(A)` is the same unary `@` as `@A`, over a group
# (l2_address_node). swap may write A's place through it, so `call: A` has no proved body: refused at the call, not
# run by A's ABI over B (formerly "a trampoline was called outside its method's signature" at run time).
int: status 7
A:
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 9; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
end: A
B:
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: status; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
end: B
fn: swap (@@: p Lmx) int
    \p: B
    return: 0
end: swap
int: k swap(@(A))
call: A
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 90; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
